> processx-connection.c:1275:3: internal compiler error: Illegal instruction

> utf8lite/src/array.c:71:3: internal compiler error: Illegal instruction

> /opt/gnu/gcc/include/c++/7.2.0/limits:1599:7: internal compiler error: Illegal instruction

> arg.c:37:5: internal compiler error: Illegal instruction

> modp_numtoa.c:134:2: internal compiler error: Illegal instruction

These errors should never happen on a system that's operating
correctly.  They indicate either a problem with the *hardware* (e.g.
faulty RAM or CPU), or severe corruption of the base operating system.
You should take this up with whoever maintains the computers you are
using.

zw

